      {
        "id": 200939,
        "name": "dprcooke",
        "username": "dprcooke",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/{size}/1961_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-03T20:32:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, what would happen if someone took Fanatic's Aegis and Sword along with how powerful Citizen Truth's shield is to stop a Relic. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I remember them mentioning (in the Dawn episode?) that Citizen Truth's shield is very powerful because it is specifically tied to his will. &nbsp;And since his will is so very strong/indomitable, so is the shield. &nbsp;\"If his will is unshaking then the shield is unbreaking\" was their explanation IIRC.</p>",
