      {
        "id": 200941,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-06T01:04:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't think they've been consistent about that. &nbsp;We know that Absolution, for instance, only has power because Fanatic believes it should. &nbsp;I don't think it would work for anything else. &nbsp;But they also suggested that the \"Relic\" keyword is more about how resistant to destruction the item in question is, and we know the instruments get destroyed all the time.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The impression I got was that while Fanatic imbued her sword with power, that power was accessible to anyone who wielded the sword. &nbsp;In contrast with the Virtuoso instruments, which are useless to anyone other than another Virtuoso (unless you like listening to pretty music, of course)</p>",
